    "analystNotes": "The Angels are the largest number in baseball's 2026 sale market: Stan Kroenke agreed on Sept 1, 2026 to buy Arte Moreno's controlling interest at a reported ~$4B, a 43% premium to the $2.8B Forbes mark from March and a record for an MLB club, with closing expected in the first quarter of 2027. Forbes counts $377M of revenue and a $14M operating loss for a 62-98 team with no playoff trip since 2014, so Kroenke is paying for the Los Angeles market and roughly 130 acres of publicly owned parking around Angel Stadium, not the roster. The club bought out Main Street's half of its RSN and relaunched it as Angels Broadcast Television in May 2026, keeping local rights in house through the FanDuel collapse. Rendon is paid off through 2030, Trout has $141.8M left through 2030, and the stadium land deal Kroenke negotiates with Anaheim is what turns $4B into a rational price.",
