    "analystNotes": "Forbes valued the Jets at $1.05B in December 2024 on $170M of revenue, 31st in the league, and the season that followed was the best in franchise history: a first Presidents' Trophy at 116 points in 2024-25 before a second-round loss to Dallas, followed by a 35-35-12 collapse and a 2026 miss. True North answered by paying Kyle Connor $12M a year through 2033-34 (signed October 8, 2025), locking Connor, Scheifele and Hellebuyck through at least 2030-31 in the NHL's smallest building. The C$11B Rogers national deal starting 2026-27 is the one revenue line that grows regardless of a 950,000-person metro, and it is what lifts this floor.",
